Z||000005||fiero56||01-09-2000||11:00 PM||||This is surprising. I've e-mailed them several times, requesting more information, questions, etc. and have always received very friendly and informative answers. When I call their phone number they always answer on the first two rings and always seem friendly. I'm not saying TOM is a lier, I believe what he says what they said. But it seems very out of character for them. If what they said was totally unprovoked I too, am going to question my further business with them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TOM||01-10-2000||12:00 AM||||I too have done business with them and was very happy with the transactions. I was shocked when I got this reply. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||01-10-2000||12:17 AM||||When posing an e-mail quote, especially one like this, please copy the entire message. Include the headers if posible. (exactly how you display the headers depends on what e-mail program you use. Headers include things besides the complete sender address. makes it harder for the sender to deny it was them.)<P>Actually I'm not suprised at this responce. Much of their pricing reflects a profiteering attitude. They are often grosely over local parts stores for many common items. Many of the prices for other things are jacked up even over Pontiac Dealer pricing. I grant they do have some hard to find things, but they are really sticking it to people on allot of stuff.<P>As far as the nice responces..... they bloody better be. they are charging enough for their product. But then most con men are nice when it suites them.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||william_thorniii||01-10-2000||02:26 AM||||Everyone knows that the Fiero Store has high prices.  Although on some things they are more reasonable than individual owners.  Unfortunately for a business to only have parts for cars at a minimum of 12 years old that might be the only way to stay in business.  I think that the message that Tom received is unfortunate, but I find it rather difficult to believe that there is not more to this situation (on their end) than we know.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||11
Z||000009||dogtired||01-10-2000||02:50 AM||||Sounds like someone was having a BAD day???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>It doesn't matter if a company is large or small they still have to be customer oriented, if they have any desire to stay in business.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I personally have never purchased anything from them, but sure like having them there as a resource??<BR>This will certainly move them from one list to the other  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||01-10-2000||11:13 AM||||I've always had good luck buying from the Fiero Store.  Among other purchases, I got my KYB shocks/struts for the 88 from them.  They screwed up and sent me the 84-87 style.  When I called them, they immediately shipped me the right style and a return packing label to send the 84-87 shocks/struts back, which I did ASAP.  Most companies would have either charged my card for both sets of shocks, then refunded when they got the wrong ones back, but not the Fiero Store - they trusted me.<P>Tom, my guess is they hired one a$$hole, and you had the bad luck to have to deal with him.  Hope he gets fired soon.||||reg||1
Z||000011||william_thorniii||01-12-2000||12:10 AM||||Guys,<P>This came through on the fiero one-list.  I thought that it was relevant.  <P>From: William Zishka &lt;dream9@pacbell.net&gt; Save Address Block Sender<BR>To: Fiero List &lt;fiero-list@fiero.org&gt;, FIERO@onelist.com Save Address <BR>Subject: [FIERO] Fiero Store Custome Service<BR>Date: Sun, 09 Jan 2000 22:20:01 -0800Reply 	Reply All 	Forward	Delete	Previous	Next	Close<BR>From: William Zishka &lt;dream9@pacbell.net&gt;<P>When things go well I like to tell people about my experience. I just<BR>want<BR>everyone to know that I am 100% satisfied with the service at the<BR>Connecticut Fiero Store. Not long ago I purchased a performance engine<BR>rebuild kit from these guys and all was going together well but I was<BR>concerned about the camshaft. So I asked my wife to call one morning as<BR>I<BR>was leaving for the office. My question was "Did I have the correct cam<BR>for<BR>an automatic transmission. Turns out they didn't send the correct cam<BR>after<BR>all. They had mistakenly sent a stock cam instead of the performance<BR>cam.<BR>The guys at the Fiero Store shipped the performance cam that same day<BR>with<BR>instructions to return the stock cam when I am able. The project is<BR>finished<BR>now and thanks to an alert Fiero Store employee I have the motor I was<BR>expecting and not something else. People say the parts from the Fiero<BR>Store<BR>are over priced but with customer service like this I think it is worth<BR>the<BR>price.<P>Bill Z<BR>Irvine, California<P>'84 Sliver 2M4 Sports Coupe 140 hp duke<BR>'84 Bright Red SE 2M4 WS6 auto<BR>'86 Silver/Black SE 2M4 Y99 5 speed<P>--<BR>This list is proudly sponsored by:<P>The Fiero Factory - 8710B Hwy 53, Toney, AL 35773<BR>Parts, Service, Fieros for sale! - <A HREF="http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory" TARGET=_blank>http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory</A> <BR>Days: 256-420-5391    Nites: 256-882-1568<P>Contact the list moderator at:  FIERO-owner@onelist.com||||reg||4
Z||000012||superXmotorsports||01-12-2000||07:47 AM||||I'm sorry to hear about your rude response you got from them Tom.  I order something from them at least once a month and for the last year and a half I've never had a problem.  My parts almost always arrive in 2 -4 days which is MUCH better than a few other sources I have used.  And they never rip me off on shipping either what they charge you is what is printed on the package.  I've just started dealing w/ eBay and it looks like it could cause extra frustration for anybody.  Thanks all. SXM.||||reg||2
